.TH QREPL 1 "November 2026" "Qore ncurses 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qrepl \- interactive Qore shell with a terminal user interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qrepl
.RI [ \-\-help | \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qrepl
runs Qore expressions in an interactive terminal interface built with NcursesUi.
It provides an input prompt, output scrolling, command history, completion,
menus and dialogs. It requires a terminal described by the TERM environment
variable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE USE
Press Enter to evaluate Qore expressions. Evaluation runs in the background;
output continues to arrive while the editor and menus remain usable.
The status bar shows whether evaluation is running or output following is paused.
The prompt follows the latest output; once the screen fills, output scrolls above it.
.TP
.B Tab
Show completion choices and signature help for the current session.
.TP
.B F1
Show keyboard help. Use /help or /? for scrollable Qore command help, starting at the beginning.
Arrows, PageUp/PageDown and Home/End scroll; Escape closes the help.
.TP
.B F6
Switch between the editor and output. In output, Home pauses following and End
resumes following new output.
.TP
.B Alt+F
Open the File menu. Load selects a source file; Save prompts for a filename and
confirms before overwriting an existing file.
.TP
.B /exit, /quit, /q, Ctrl+Q or Alt+Q
Exit immediately while idle. File > Quit does the same. Unfinished input does
not require saving. During evaluation, a confirmation offers to finish and then
exit; this does not cancel the evaluated code.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Exit on empty input; otherwise delete the character after the cursor.
.TP
.B Esc
Dismiss the current menu or dialog without exiting.
.SH BACKGROUND THREADS
/threads lists IDs and names in the current Program. /cancel <tid|all> requests
cooperative termination; /join <tid|all> waits for threads to leave the Program.
Parsing, /type, /load, /reset and exit require an idle Program. While threads are
active, choose Wait, Cancel request or Terminate threads. Completion closes the
dialog and resumes the request automatically. Cancel preserves input and leaves
the threads running. Cancellation can be caught or deferred by evaluated code.
This workflow requires Qore 3.0 with Program thread coordination and its matching
QoreRepl module.
.SH MULTILINE INPUT
At the continuation prompt, every line is Qore source, including slash-prefixed
lines and history shortcuts. Commands are available at the primary qore> prompt.
Press Ctrl+C with no editor selection to cancel unfinished input and return to
that prompt without resetting the Program. With selected text, Ctrl+C copies it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
Terminal type used by ncurses to select its terminal capabilities.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qore (1),
.BR terminfo (5)
.PP
The qore-ncurses-module-doc package provides the terminal and widget API
references and test examples.
